WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
Four non-person identities
carry the integration.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:07.387
SailPoint's Entra connector app
registration in the agency's tenant.

3
00:00:07.387 --> 00:00:10.113
The ServiceNow Entra
spoke's app registration.

4
00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:14.522
The ServiceNow integration user
that SailPoint's workflow posts as,

5
00:00:14.522 --> 00:00:19.163
together with the verifier account
the re-read client closes records as.

6
00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:22.888
And the SailPoint API client
the kit's clients read with.

7
00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:25.773
As design guidance, each
has two named owners

8
00:00:25.773 --> 00:00:28.737
and a federal sponsor in
the system inventory.

9
00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:29.901
Now the flows.

10
00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:34.472
SailPoint's cloud connectors call
Microsoft Graph from SailPoint's cloud;

11
00:00:34.472 --> 00:00:39.338
only the Active Directory path runs
through its on-premises virtual appliance.

12
00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:44.312
And, by inference, its workflows call
out from SailPoint's cloud to ServiceNow.

13
00:00:44.312 --> 00:00:49.183
The Federal Modernization Workbook's design
prefers execution through a connector

14
00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:53.640
inside the boundary, so each vendor-cloud
action becomes a recorded data flow.
